<title>USA: Vision-Sciences executives buy more shares.</title>
<headline>Vision-Sciences executives buy more shares.</headline>
<dateline>NATICK, Mass. 1996-12-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Vision-Sciences Inc said Tuesday that it has completed a $2 million private placement with Katsumi Oneda, its chairman, chief executive and president, and Lewis Pell, its vice chairman.</p>
<p>Oneda and Pell each have bought 842,105 common shares at $1.1875 per share. Oneda now beneficially owns about 23.5 percent of the company's outstanding common shares, and Pell beneficially owns about 22 percent, the company said.</p>
</text>
